     raise-exit)\n          routed (if (::invoker env)\n                   (u/if-node\n                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/map?) (u/v callee))\n                                (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) (u/v callee) (u/lit :yang.call/entry))\n                                           (u/lit true)\n                                           ;; the shape is only WHEN to ask (ruling of\n                                           ;; record, rule 2): the heap answers\n                                           ;; `cell/authentic?`, and an unauthenticated\n                                           ;; shape takes ordinary map invocation\n                                           (u/if-node (cell-ref-shaped-node (u/v callee))\n                                                      (u/app (u/v 'cell/authentic?) (u/v callee))\n                                                      (u/lit false)))\n                                (u/lit false))\n                     admitted\n                     value-call)\n                   admitted)]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:845:;; to `clj/try`/`clj/try-finally` (the `%capture` handler-stack family), and a\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:883:;; encoding: a `%capture` handler stack in a dynamic-context cell, exactly\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:899:   break/continue/return escapes). The handler stack is a chain of frames\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:900:   [tag payload rest n]; a `:handler` frame holds the continuation\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:901:   `clj/raise` delivers to, a `:finally` frame a one-argument thunk every\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:903:  '[[clj/ctx (fn [hs] (dsg__assoc {} :handlers hs))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:904:    [clj/handlers (fn [] (dsg__get (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:905:    [clj/set-handlers!\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:907:       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (dsg__assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers hs)))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:917:             